{
	title: 'Notice text from the model: final summary and mid-turn notify',
	spec: "The system prompt asks the model to end a final answer with <summary>…</summary>, at most 80 characters, the one line a notice shows; clients strip it from the shown answer and the notice uses it instead of the reply's last line (absent tag: last line as before). A notify tool with one text argument posts a notice mid-turn (for example when the user asked to be told if the approach fails); it routes like any notice and answers 'sent'. The final summary is a tag, not a tool, because a tool call at the end of a turn costs another request; mid-turn the turn goes on anyway, so a tool is free and structured.",
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['qm']
}
